{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\nimport sys\nimport math\nimport itertools\n\noriginal_stdout = sys.stdout\nuse_file_io = False\n\nif use_file_io:\n    fin = open('input.txt', 'r')\n    fout = open('output.txt', 'w')\n    sys.stdout = fout\n    def read_line():\n        return fin.readline().strip()\nelse:\n    fin = sys.stdin\n    fout = sys.stdout\n    def read_line():\n        return fin.buffer.readline().strip()\n\ndef read_int_list():\n    return list(map(int, read_line().split()))\n\ndef read_int():\n    return int(read_line())\n\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef mod_pow(base, exp):\n    result = 1\n    while exp:\n        if exp & 1:\n            result = (result * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n    return result\n\ndef factorial(n):\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        result = (result * i) % MOD\n    return result\n\ndef solve():\n    n = read_int()\n    a = read_int_list()\n    b = read_int_list()\n    a1, a2, a3 = a\n    b1, b2, b3 = b\n    \n    max_possible = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1)\n    \n    best_match = 0\n    for perm in itertools.permutations([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]):\n        ta1, ta2, ta3 = a1, a2, a3\n        tb1, tb2, tb3 = b1, b2, b3\n        current_match = 0\n        \n        for p in perm:\n            if p == 1:\n                t = min(ta1, tb1)\n                ta1 -= t\n                tb1 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 2:\n                t = min(ta1, tb3)\n                ta1 -= t\n                tb3 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 3:\n                t = min(ta2, tb2)\n                ta2 -= t\n                tb2 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 4:\n                t = min(ta2, tb1)\n                ta2 -= t\n                tb1 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 5:\n                t = min(ta3, tb3)\n                ta3 -= t\n                tb3 -= t\n                current_match += t\n            elif p == 6:\n                t = min(ta3, tb2)\n                ta3 -= t\n                tb2 -= t\n                current_match += t\n        \n        best_match = max(best_match, current_match)\n    \n    print(n - best_match, mx := max_possible)\n\ndef main():\n    try:\n        t = 1\n        for _ in range(t):\n            solve()\n    finally:\n        fin.close()\n        fout.close()\n        sys.stdout = original_stdout\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <climits>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007;\n\nlong long mod_pow(long long base, long long exp) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) {\n            result = (result * base) % MOD;\n        }\n        exp >>= 1;\n        base = (base * base) % MOD;\n    }\n    return